# FDA shoulder source and ingestion status

The [FDA shoulder tool](https://cdrh-rst.fda.gov/human-shoulder-finite-element-model)
is a promising independent reference for missing joint soft tissues. It has not
been admitted into the Atlas or fitted to its existing shoulder. This inventory
does not establish clinical accuracy, laterality, units or patient-space alignment.

## Exact source

[Publisher repository](https://github.com/OSEL-DAM/ShoulderFiniteElementModel/tree/fc9f3e56b104c06759750495be1f8dd5d53c1741),
commit `fc9f3e56b104c06759750495be1f8dd5d53c1741`.
The repository LICENSE and Word model notes both declare CC0-1.0. The exact
LICENSE SHA256 is `a2010f343487d3f7618affe54f789f5487602331c0a8d03f49e9a7c547cf0499`.
The model notes SHA256 is `9f5a5140224b95933edead95be5a5612544e0828f73b9be0e13836db2ee7511a`.
This is component-specific evidence, not a licence conclusion for unrelated FDA
or NIH files. Preserve the publisher's disclaimers and credit; do not imply FDA
endorsement or regulatory qualification. No solver, commercial software purchase
or execution of downloaded code was needed for this text inventory.

`Male-Shoulder.inp` is 59,793,091 bytes, SHA256
`547de9cff23a4ae98d5a297ba32d8b01fe042739160c4b7144dfe7066d08c70a`.
Its complete source, licence and notes are retained in local quarantine only;
none is redistributed by this source-only tooling change.

## Actual file inventory

| Source part | Nodes | C3D10M elements | Publisher-described geometry origin |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| AC_Lig | 3,211 | 2,111 | CT segmentation |
| CLAVICLE | 30,567 | 16,511 | CT segmentation |
| Gcart | 56,257 | 36,551 | Constructed offset cartilage |
| Hcart | 119,844 | 73,736 | Constructed offset cartilage |
| Humerus | 68,491 | 39,827 | CT segmentation |
| Labrum | 177,134 | 124,307 | CT segmentation |
| SCAPULA | 103,447 | 55,349 | CT segmentation |

These are seven finite-element parts, not seven newly approved Atlas structures.
Nineteen assembly connector elements are not muscle surfaces. The model is from
one male Visible Human donor and a constrained abduction experiment, not normal
motion or patient-specific simulation. The [NLM source page](https://www.nlm.nih.gov/research/visible/visible_human.html)
describes the underlying public-domain donor image collection.

## Reproduce and preserve the boundary

```text
node --test scripts/test-abaqus-shoulder-source.mjs
node scripts/inspect-abaqus-shoulder-source.mjs <local-pinned-Male-Shoulder.inp>
```

The reader validates the exact input, part/node/element identities, finite
coordinates, ten-node connectivity and references. It refuses unsupported mesh
types, external includes, parameters and part coordinate transforms. It records
instance translation/axis-angle rows separately and does not apply them, emit
surfaces or infer a millimetre frame. Humerus and Hcart have non-identity assembly
transforms. A separate load-axis transform is reported, not mistaken for a mesh
registration. Bounds remain explicitly raw-part bounds.

The conversion below verifies ordering and placement fixtures and records the
implemented geometry checks. Before a learner-facing reference, resolve its
remaining unit, coordinate, topology and anatomical validation requirements and
generate a separate source-ID catalogue with exact notices and revision-bound
Review. Do not substitute the connectors for rotator-cuff meshes, infer missing
capsule/bursae/other ligaments, reuse existing body IDs or transfer approvals.
BodyParts3D and scan registration remain independently unvalidated.

## Converted quarantine surfaces

The separate conversion tools now extract boundary faces using the official
[tetrahedron node layout](https://docs.software.vt.edu/abaqusv2025/English/SIMACAEELMRefMap/simaelm-r-3delem.htm)
and apply source instance placement in the documented
[translation then rotation order](https://docs.software.vt.edu/abaqusv2025/English/SIMACAEKEYRefMap/simakey-r-instance.htm).
Each six-node face becomes four linear triangles using its existing corner and
midside coordinates. This is node-sampled geometry, not the exact continuous
quadratic surface, a solver result or a repaired mesh. OBJ doubles and source-ID
maps remain in an external local quarantine, outside the source checkout.

| Part | Boundary vertices | Sampled triangles | Implemented topology audit |
| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |
| AC_Lig | 798 | 1,592 | Closed oriented vertex manifold |
| Gcart | 15,956 | 31,912 | Hold: two nonmanifold edges and three vertices |
| Hcart | 44,686 | 89,368 | Closed oriented vertex manifold |
| Labrum | 26,476 | 52,952 | Closed oriented vertex manifold |
| CLAVICLE | 16,494 | 32,984 | Closed oriented vertex manifold |
| Humerus | 30,598 | 61,192 | Closed oriented vertex manifold |
| SCAPULA | 58,326 | 116,648 | Closed oriented vertex manifold |

Gcart source nodes `2798`, `4501` and `37871` retain their original coordinates
and abnormal vertex links. No smoothing, deletion, welding or decimation was
used to hide them. The seven surfaces total 386,648 triangles. Self-intersections
and anatomical attachments have not been validated; passing the stated graph
checks is not clinical acceptance or a watertight-solid simulation guarantee.

Independent readback reconstructs every source face and OBJ triangle, checks all
source-node positions against independently computed instance placement, and
rejects rehashed geometry/identity edits and forged approval/healthy flags. The
five untransformed parts retain exact parsed source coordinates; the two rotated
parts differ from the independent arithmetic oracle by at most approximately
`1.14e-13` in unverified source coordinate values, not millimetres.

```text
node --test scripts/test-abaqus-shoulder-source.mjs scripts/test-abaqus-instance-transform.mjs scripts/test-abaqus-quadratic-boundary.mjs
node scripts/convert-pinned-fda-shoulder.mjs <local-pinned-Male-Shoulder.inp> <NEW-external-quarantine-directory>
node scripts/check-fda-shoulder-surface-readback.mjs <local-pinned-Male-Shoulder.inp> <quarantine-directory>
node scripts/test-fda-shoulder-surface-readback.mjs <local-pinned-Male-Shoulder.inp> <quarantine-directory>
```

The [authors' abstract](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35882682/) describes a
right shoulder. That is publisher-reported laterality, not independent validation
of model axes, an invitation to mirror it or permission to claim spatial linkage
to the existing Atlas. Current conversion metadata keeps laterality and units
unverified. Establish the coordinate convention/units, investigate the retained
Gcart defects, audit intersections and anatomical fidelity, and create an exact
source-specific catalogue/Review binding before any learner admission. Preserve
all independent source holds and constructed-cartilage distinctions.
